## FOUND

**The P1 this round claims to have closed is not closed.** `V74C-D1`'s fix replaced a bare-stem test with a **blocklist of six Mongolian ending families**. The verbal paradigm has about thirty; the imperative paradigm has five. Generated 14 stems × 28 form families = **392 tokens** and ran them through the real predicate lifted from the deploy bytes: **195 read as live imperatives** — `архивлахгүй` ("will not archive"), `архивлаагүй` ("was not archived"), `архивлалаа`, `архивлана`, `архивлаж`, `архивлагч` (a *noun*), `архивлавал`, `архивлажээ`. On 10 matched turn pairs, **10 of 10 Mongolian refusal turns stop being whole-turn refusals** while the identical English turn is stripped — so `index.ts:4195` leaves the model's `archiveCompanyIds` in place and the write the founder forbade reaches the executor. Third round running, same language.

